values ('ap_physics_2', 11, '11.3', array['11.3']::text[], 'convention', 'Ohmic materials and the I–ΔV graph', 'Ohmic materials have constant resistance for all currents, and the resistance of an ohmic element is found from the slope of its graph of current versus potential difference.', '[]'::jsonb, NULL, 'On a graph of I (vertical) versus ΔV (horizontal), the slope equals 1/R, not R.', 'published', 'generated-checked; extractor=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; batch=ap-physics-2-reference-u9-u11-2026-10-10; candidate=ap_physics_2-u11-r1-013; ced=11.3.B.1.i "Materials that obey Ohm''s law have constant resistance for all currents"; 11.3.B.1.iv')
