values ('ap_physics_2', 11, '11.8', array['11.8']::text[], 'list_sequence', 'Charging capacitor: initial to final state', 'How an initially uncharged capacitor behaves from the moment it is placed in a circuit until steady state.', '[{"label": "Immediately after connection", "meaning": "Uncharged capacitor acts like a wire; charge flows easily to the plates"}, {"label": "While charging", "meaning": "Capacitor potential difference, plate charge, and stored energy change over time and asymptotically approach steady state; branch current also changes"}, {"label": "After a long time (t >> τ)", "meaning": "Fully charged, with maximum potential difference and zero current in the capacitor''s branch"}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'Describe these states qualitatively; no mathematical model with respect to time is expected.', 'published', 'generated-checked; extractor=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; batch=ap-physics-2-reference-u9-u11-2026-10-10; candidate=ap_physics_2-u11-r1-037; ced=11.8.B.2.i; 11.8.B.2.iv "zero current in the circuit branch"; boundary statement')
